{"title":"Science","timeMinutes":8,"questions":[{"text":"What is the Chandrasekhar limit?","image":"","options":["5 solar masses","1.4 solar masses","2.5 solar masses","3.14 solar masses"],"correctIdx":1},{"text":"What do scientists study in Antarctic ice chambers?","image":"","options":["Neutrinos","Quarks Behaviour","Ice Cream Recipe","Leptons"],"correctIdx":0},{"text":"Which enzyme unwinds DNA during replication?","image":"","options":["Helicase","Pepsin","Ligase","Amylase"],"correctIdx":0},{"text":"Which planet has the shortest day?","image":"","options":["Earth","Mars","Neptune","Jupiter"],"correctIdx":3},{"text":"What is the approximate temperature of the Sun's core?","image":"","options":["15 crore K","15 billion K","15 trillion K","15 million K"],"correctIdx":3},{"text":"What is the SI unit of catalytic activity?","image":"","options":["Kives","JJBA","Katal","Bakayarou"],"correctIdx":2},{"text":"Which part of the brain regulates body temperature?","image":"","options":["Baby Brain","Hypothalamus","Cerebellum","None of These"],"correctIdx":1},{"text":"Which phenomenon explains light bending around massive objects?","image":"","options":["Polarization","Death Ray","Gravitational lensing","Radio Diffusion"],"correctIdx":2},{"text":"Which gas is used in many cryogenic experiments to reach extremely low temperatures?","image":"","options":["Helium","Radon","Gobar Gas","Xenon"],"correctIdx":0},{"text":"What is the purpose of a gyroscope in spacecraft?","image":"","options":["Carry Weight","To Walk","Generate Thrust","Measure/Maintain orientation"],"correctIdx":3},{"text":"Which blood vessel carries oxygenated blood from the lungs to the heart?","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["Inferior vena cava","Pulmonary vein","Pulmonary artery","Superior vena cava"],"correctIdx":1},{"text":"What does the term Dolby B or Dolby C printed\non tape recorders and other sound systems refer\nto?","image":"","options":["company name","frequency modulated system","noise reduction circuit","amplitude modulated system"],"correctIdx":2},{"text":"Who is he?","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["James Watson","Alfred Nobel","Salman Khan","Nikola Tesla"],"correctIdx":3},{"text":"A piece of ice is foating in a beaker containing\nwater. When whole of the ice melts:","image":"","options":["level of water come up","level of water goes down","first rise then fall","level of water remains same"],"correctIdx":3},{"text":"Traditional gunpowder (black powder) is made from","image":"","options":["Sodium sulphate","Potassium nitrate","Calcium Carbonate","potassium perchlorate"],"correctIdx":1},{"text":"If a liquid is heated in space under no gravity, the transfer of heat will take place by process of","image":"","options":["conduction","convection","radiation","cannot be heated in the absence of gravity"],"correctIdx":2},{"text":"CHCL3 is","image":"","options":["Chloroform","Methane","Bleaching Powder","Soda"],"correctIdx":0},{"text":"Total no of constilations","image":"","options":["12","88","106","80"],"correctIdx":1},{"text":"What is this instrument?","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["Astrolabe","Torquetum","Antikythera Mechanism","Sun Dial"],"correctIdx":0},{"text":"What Endorphin do?","image":"","options":["Make antibodies","Cause irritation","Relieve pain","Cause stress"],"correctIdx":2}]}